---
import Layout from '../../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="Mineral Wool Insulation — Non-Combustible Facade Insulation" description="House insulation with mineral wool — non-combustible, vapor-permeable thermal insulation. ETICS system with stone wool. Installation Krakow and Malopolska." schemaType="services" locale="en">
  <section class="relative pt-32 pb-16 bg-slate-900 overflow-hidden">
    <div class="absolute inset-0"><div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-b from-slate-900/80 via-slate-900/95 to-slate-900"></div></div>
    <div class="absolute top-0 left-0 w-full h-1.5 bg-red-600"></div>
    <div class="relative max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-slate-400 mb-8"><a href="/en" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/en/services" class="hover:text-white transition-colors">Services</a><span>/</span><span class="text-orange-400">Mineral Wool Insulation</span></nav>
      <div class="text-center max-w-4xl mx-auto">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full bg-orange-500/10 border border-orange-500/20 mb-6"><span class="text-orange-400 text-sm font-semibold">Non-Combustible Insulation</span></div>
        <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-extrabold text-white tracking-tight">Mineral Wool <span class="text-gradient">Insulation</span></h1>
        <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-slate-400 max-w-2xl mx-auto leading-relaxed">Stone mineral wool — non-combustible A1 class insulation with excellent vapor permeability. Safe, durable, and acoustically effective. Mandatory for buildings over 25 meters high.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding bg-white">
    <div class="max-w-7xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-slate-900 mb-6">What is <span class="text-gradient">mineral wool insulation</span>?</h2>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">Mineral wool (stone wool) insulation is a building thermal modernization system using basalt wool boards as insulation material. Stone mineral wool is made by melting basalt rocks at over 1500 degrees C — making it completely non-combustible and classified as fire reaction class A1.</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed mb-6">In the ETICS system, mineral wool is bonded and anchored to external walls, then finished with a reinforcement layer and exterior plaster. A key advantage of wool is its high vapor permeability — it allows walls to "breathe," which is particularly important for older buildings with damp walls.</p>
        <p class="text-lg text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">Polish fire regulations require non-combustible insulation in buildings over 25 m high. Additionally, mineral wool is an excellent acoustic insulator — it reduces external noise much more effectively than polystyrene.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-padding bg-slate-900">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 lg:px-8 text-center">
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-extrabold text-white mb-6">Insulate your home with <span class="text-gradient">mineral wool</span></h2>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">Fire safety, vapor permeability, and quiet — mineral wool is an investment in comfort and safety. Contact us for a free quote.</p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a href="/en/contact" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-red-600 hover:bg-red-500 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl transition-colors">Free insulation quote</a>
        <a href="tel:+48515156233" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-semibold rounded-xl border border-white/20 transition-colors">Call: 515-156-233</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
